    "order": 1,
    "heading": "REQUIREMENT FOR EFFECTIVE PRAYER:",
    "body": "You should pray in the name of Jesus (John 14:13-14, John 16:23-24) Righteousness (Psalm 34:15, Isaiah 59:1-2, Psalm 66:18-20, Mark 11:25, Isaiah 64:6) Holy Spirit (Rom 8:26-27) Our prayer must be according to Godâs will (James 4:1-6, Psalm 66:18) Faith (James 1:5-8, Matt 11:23-24) Persistence (Luke 18:1-7, Col 4:2, I Thess 5:17) Fasting (Neh 1:9, Dan 9:3-4, Matt 6:16, Mark 9:29) REASONS WHY ANSWER MAY BE DELAYED- The will of God and the Timing We pray to know the will of God and that the will of God should to pass in our lives. At times, our pray may be the will of God for our lives, but the time for the fulfilment is not ripe. There is time for everything (Eccl 3:1). The children of Israel were promised salvation though Jesus Christ, until Christ was born that the promise was fulfilled (Luke 2:25-32). (Hab 2:3)",
    "sub_points": []
  }
]

