[
  {
    "order": 1,
    "heading": "AWON IBASEPO IGBALODE",
    "body": "Igbeyawo ti o sile: Eleyi iru igbeyawo ti adehun wa larin okunrin ati obinrin wipe awon le ni enikeni miran lati ni ibalopo pelu, ti enikeji o si gbodo jowu.. Omiran ni igbeyawo oni adehun wipe okunrin ati obirin na yio fe ara won fun igba die (won o ti jo mo iye odun na), won o si pinya. Enikeni ninu awon mejeji le san owo fun enikeji nigbati won ba pin. Igbeyawo ti okunrin kan yi o fe obirin meji, meta, merin ati bebelo. Igbeyawo ti obirin kan yi o fe okunrin meji, meta, merin ati bebelo. Igbeyawo ti obirin meji fe ara won. Igbeyawo ti okunrin meji fe ara won.",
    "sub_points": []
  },
  {
    "order": 2,
    "heading": "PATAKI IGBEYAWO",
    "body": "Fun ajumokegbe: Eleyi ni lati ni eniyan lati ba jiroro, ki won si jo ni Alafia papo. Awon igbeyawo igbalode yi le gba alafia eyikeyi ninu awon ti won jo wa ninu ibasepo yi. Fun omo bibi: Igbeyawo je igbekale lati mu eto Olorun nipa ibisi se. Eto Olorun nipe omo yio ma waye lati ara okunrin ati obirin laisi agbere ati pansaga. Awon miran lara awon eto igbeyawo igbalode yi kole mu eyi se. . O je ona lati sa fun agbere. Ara idi ti igbeyawo fi waye ni ki a te ara wa lorun nipa ibalopo. Okunrin kan ati obirin kan. Awon miran ninu awon ilana igbeyawo igbalode yi nran agbere ati pansaga lowo. (1 Kor 7:12)",
    "sub_points": []
  },
  {
    "order": 3,
    "heading": "IGBEYAWO TI OLORUN LA KALE:",
    "body": "Okunrin kan ati Obirin kan, ki won si di okan (Matt 19:4-5) Awon meeji yio jo gbepo lati te ara won lorun (1 Kor 7:3-4) Awon mejeeji jo gba pe irin ajo titi lailai ni, titi iku yio fi ya won (Matt 19:8) Ti awon mejeeji je orison itunu fun ara won (Gen 24:67) Ti okunrin ati Obirin mu itunu ba awon obi awon mejeeji (Gen 26:34-35)",
    "sub_points": []
  }
]

[
  {
    "order": 1,
    "heading": "MODERN UNIONS",
    "body": "Open Marriage: This is an agreement to marry and each partner can have any other sex partners, any other married partners should not be jealous. Contract marriage: An agreement to marry for some years and they part ways. Any of the partners can pay the other off depending on the person bringing the idea. Polygamy: A union in which man married more than a woman. Polyandry: A union in which a woman married more than a man Lesbianism: A union in which two women married themselves. Gayism: A union in which two men married themselves.",
    "sub_points": []
  },
  {
    "order": 2,
    "heading": "PURPOSE OF MARRIAGE",
    "body": "Companionship: Having someone to discuss and relate with, then enjoy peace together. Some of these new forms of marriage will take the peace of a partner away. Procreation: Marriage is designed as an establishment to fulfil Godâs plan of bringing new life to the world. The plan of God is that children are to be born through the union of the husband and wife without fornication. Some of the listed unions above cannot achieve this. To avoid fornication: The reason for marriage is to satisfy each other sexually. A man to a woman. Open marriage, polygamy and polyandry aid fornication. (1 Cor 7:12)",
    "sub_points": []
  },
  {
    "order": 3,
    "heading": "THE MARRIAGE GOD ORDAINED:",
    "body": "A man to a woman union and they become one (Matt 19:4-5) Where both live to satisfy the other (1 Cor 7:3-4) Where both accept that it is a journey of forever, till death separate them (Matt 19:8) Where both are source of comfort to each other (Gen 24:67) Where the man and the woman bring comfort to their parents (Gen 26:34-35)",
    "sub_points": []
  }
]

[
  {
    "order": 1,
    "heading": "JESUS AND THE CHURCH AS PERFECT EXAMPLE:",
    "body": "Jesus loves the church and offered himself as sacrifice for the church (Eph 5:25). As husband and wife, we should be ready to commit ourselves to the affairs of the home. Commitment is the last level of love, which is given all we have to things that pertain to the wellbeing and the future of the home. No partner should be selfish. Some partners would have eaten before coming home, and would not bother if the other partner and the children have eaten. It is not a godly behaviour.",
    "sub_points": []
  },
  {
    "order": 2,
    "heading": "UNDERSTAND THE SYSTEM THAT WORKS FOR YOU:",
    "body": "The perfect situation is to maintain same purse/account. God wants us to be one in all that we do as husband and wife, but there is another alternative, which is maintaining separate accounts. For peace to reisgn in our home, we should understand the system that would not cause conflict. The most important thing is that each partner should be honest to the other and be financially committed to the home affairs. Family should have pursuits and every member should contribute towards the achievement.",
    "sub_points": []
  }
]

[
  {
    "order": 1,
    "heading": "JESU ATI IJO GEGEBI APEERE PIPE:",
    "body": "Jesu feran ijo, o si fi ara rubo fun ijo (Efe 5:25). Gegebi oko ati iyawo, agbodo setan lati fi ara wa ji fun gbodo eto ile wa. Ifara-eni-ji je ipele ti o kehin ninu ife, o je fifi oun gbogbo ti o ni kale fun alafia ati ojo waju ile . A ko gbodo ke aladanikan je tabi onimotara eni nikan. Oko tabi Iyawo miran yio ti jeun ki o to de ile, ko si ni bikita boya enikeji re ati awon omo ti jeun. Ki i se iwa ti o ba ti Olorun mu.",
    "sub_points": []
  },
  {
    "order": 2,
    "heading": "E JO NI OYE ETO ISUNA TI YIO SISE NINU ILE YIN:",
    "body": "Eto isuna ti o dara ju ni ki e so ma lo apo ifowopamo kan na. Olorun fe ki a je okan ninu gbogbo nkan ti a ba nse gegebi oko ati iyawo, sugbon ti eleyi o ba ni sise fun wa, ki a ya apo ifowopamo wa si otooto. Ki alafia le joba ninu ile, a gbodo mo eto isuna ti ko ni fa wahala. Oun ti o se Pataki ni ki a je olooto si ara wa, ki a ni owo ninu eto isuna ile. Idile gbodo ni ilepa, gbogbo ara inu ile si gbodo ni owo ninu aseyori ilepa na.",
    "sub_points": []
  },
  {
    "order": 3,
    "heading": "LILO EKO NAA",
    "body": "Je ki o ti okan re wa lati yonda ohunkohun fun itesiwaju ile re",
    "sub_points": []
  }
]

[
  {
    "order": 1,
    "heading": "AWON OHUN TI O MA NFA WAHALA NINU ILE:",
    "body": "Aimura sile daradara fun igbeyawo Igbeaye oko ati iyawo ti ko ba ara won mu Iwa aije olooto Airi omo bi Iwa airi ifara-eni-ji Ede-aiye-de ni gbogbo igba lori igbagbo oko ati aya Didasi eto inu ile won lati odo awon obi",
