[
  {
    "order": 1,
    "heading": "CAUSES OF PROBLEMS IN HOMES:",
    "body": "Inadequate preparation for marriage Incompatibility of lifestyle Dishonest behaviour Infertility Lack of commitment Constant argument about believes Parent intrusion/interference",
    "sub_points": []
  },
  {
    "order": 2,
    "heading": "WAYSTO AVOID PROBLEM IN OUR HOMES",
    "body": "Each partner should surrender to the leading of the Holy Spirit, this will make your home an enviable one. Each partner should show love and empathy to the other as Jesus Christ showed love to the church. Christianity does not mean that we should not spice up our relationship, do things that will make your relationship to grow and strong. We should respect our partners and be committed to the relationship Lack of money or child should be taken to God in prayer. Avoid ungodly or unpleasant interference from anyone (including parents)",
    "sub_points": []
  }
]

[
  {
    "order": 1,
    "heading": "DUTIES OF THE FATHER",
    "body": "It is ordained by God that the husband should be the head of the home Ephesians 5:2, Gen. 18:19. It is the duty of the husband to love his wife as himself â Eph 5: 25, CoL3:19. This is the love expressed in 1 Corinthians 13 The husband is required to be faithful to his wife. It is the husbandâs duties to comfort his wife He ought to consult with his wife on business matters and issues that affect the home, for they are a team. The Christian husband should always put God first in his life â Luke 14: 26. He is the priest of the home and he is responsible to establish a family altar for daily worship. He is to listen and lead his wife with wise counsel â 2 Kings 4:8-10, Eccles. 4:9-11.",
    "sub_points": []
  },
  {
    "order": 2,
    "heading": "DUTIES OF THE MOTHERS IN THE HOME",
    "body": "The wife is to obey her husband â Eph 5: 22, 1 Peter 3:6. Wives are not only to respect their husbands but they are to love them too â Titus 2:4. The woman is not to be adorned with ornaments -1 Tim. 2:9-10. Instead, wives are to be adorned with good work, including modesty and sobriety, Meekness and have a quiet spirit â 1 Peter 3:4-5. A Christian wife must be trustworthy, hardworking and be an early riser Proverbs 31: 11, 13, 15.",
    "sub_points": []
  },
  {
    "order": 3,
    "heading": "THE DUTIES OF BOTH PARENTS",
    "body": "Parents are to realize that their children really belong to God (Psalm 127:3-5). Parents should bring their children to the Lord at an early age- Matthew 19:13-14 â to train and discipline them for the Lord- Proverbs 22:6. One way of making their task easy is to bring the children to Sunday School and church. Teach them Bible stories at home and give them a part in family prayers. Teach them to obey God and the law of the country â Deut. 32:46. Parents are to provide for their children- 1 Tim.5:8 â and should be careful not to provoke their children to wrath â Ephesians 6:4. Above all, let godly parents pray for their children. Pray that they would be saved to overcome sin.",
    "sub_points": []
  },
  {
    "order": 4,
    "heading": "THE DUTIES OF THE CHILDREN",
    "body": "Children are to honour their parents â Exodus 20: 12, obey them Luke 2:51, and pray for them. They must also return their parentâs love, for love is a two-way traffic. They must be sober and show good examples in all things â Titus 2:6-7. Children must constantly remember that the children of today shall be the parents of tomorrow.",
    "sub_points": []
  }
]

